### Finally, the kinetic energy

Now we make the full expression for the kinetic energy explicit using vector notation. 
$$
\begin{aligned}
T
= \frac{m}{2} \dot{\vec{R}}^2 + \frac{1}{2} \overline{\overline{I}} \vec{\Omega}^2
= \frac{m}{2} \dot{\vec{R}}^{\mathrm{tr}} \dot{\vec{R}} &+ \frac{1}{2} \vec{\Omega}^{\mathrm{tr}} \overline{\overline{I}} \vec{\Omega}\\
T = \frac{m}{2} 
\begin{pmatrix}
\dot{R}_x & \dot{R}_y & \dot{R}_z \\
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
\dot{R}_x \\
\dot{R}_y \\
\dot{R}_z \\
\end{pmatrix} 
&+
\frac{1}{2} 
\begin{pmatrix}
\Omega_x &
\Omega_y &
\Omega_z \\
\end{pmatrix} 
\begin{pmatrix}
I_{xx} & I_{xy} & I_{xz} \\
I_{yx} & I_{yy} & I_{yz} \\
I_{zx} & I_{zy} & I_{zz} \\
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
\Omega_x \\
\Omega_y \\
\Omega_z \\
\end{pmatrix}
\\ 
T = \frac{m}{2} 
\left(
\dot{R}_x^2 + \dot{R}_y^2 + \dot{R}_z^2 
\right) 
&+
\frac{1}{2}
\begin{pmatrix}
\Omega_x &
\Omega_y &
\Omega_z \\
\end{pmatrix} 
\begin{pmatrix}
I_{xx} & I_{xy} & I_{xz} \\
I_{yx} & I_{yy} & I_{yz} \\
I_{zx} & I_{zy} & I_{zz} \\
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
\Omega_x \\
\Omega_y \\
\Omega_z \\
\end{pmatrix} 
\\ 
\end{aligned}
$$

